[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1583","stub":{"id":"1583","section":"SR  271 in  Nanty Glo to Vintondale ","altname":"S. Fork Blacklick","river":"Blacklick Creek, S. Branch","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-PEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"383","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"110265","location":{"latitude":"40.4718","longitude":"-78.8359"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"115527","location":{"latitude":"40.4842","longitude":"-78.9243"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"7.1","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101251180","title":null,"post_date":"2014-06-23 04:00:00+00","detail":"6/20/14 paddle - Verify that the 2 river-wide strainers mentioned below are still there.","user":{"name":"Kelli Majiros"}},{"id":"101251089","title":null,"post_date":"2014-05-21 04:00:00+00","detail":"I ran S. B. Blacklick 16 April with Josephine @ 4160cfs and it was a rocket ride, one 2.5 mile rapid that got a bit spicy every so often. This was Twin Rocks to Rose Bud, we continued and took out at the confulence. There were two river wide strainers on the right side of islands one just above Rose Bud and one just below. Both were visible from above and we were able to eddy without issue.","user":{"name":"Randall McFarland"}}],"photos":[{"id":"791418","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791419","description":"This Ghost Town trail bridge is across the North Branch. To takeout from the South Branch you paddle across the North Branch at the confluence. Then cross this bridge carrying your boat. This puts you on SR3045 just South of Vintondale.  The Ghost Town Trail Parking is just across the road bridge.","caption":"Takout below Vintondale","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791418","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791418"}},{"id":"795232","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"795233","description":"\r\n","caption":"Jamie Brinkerhoff on the S.B. Blacklick Jan. 2010","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/795232","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/795232"}},{"id":"791260","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791261","description":"","caption":"S.B. Blacklick","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791260","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791260"}},{"id":"791269","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791270","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791269","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791269"}},{"id":"791165","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791166","description":"","caption":"S.B Blacklick","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791165","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791165"}},{"id":"791174","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791175","description":"","caption":"S.B. Blacklick","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791174","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791174"}},{"id":"791279","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791280","description":"This is just above Vintondale at the end of the run.","caption":"The Massive Vintondale Boney Pile","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791279","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791279"}},{"id":"791430","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"791431","description":"","caption":"S.B. Blacklick","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/791430","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/791430"}}],"detail":{"id":"1583","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"When the Blacklick @ Josephine hits 2000cfs the South Branch is the place to go. The prime section is tight, techincal and very busy. The reach breaks down into three parts.**Part 1:** If you putin at SR 271 in Nanty Glo you will have two miles of easy swift water though a pretty rhododendron and hemlock valley for a pleasant warm up (once you leave the levees of Nanty Glo behined).**Part 2:**The  whitewater begins after the first bridge at Twin Rocks. There is a good putin here with parking. The next 2.5 miles average a 70 ft/mi drop. The crick is pool drop, but the pools are short. **Part 3:**After the Rosebud mine bridge the crick eases up and is swift water for the next 2.5 miles to the takeout at the confluence of the North & South branches. Take out is possible at this mine access bridge but problematic as there is constant coal truck traffic across it, and and litte parking. It could enable multiple runs at the rare times when the crick is up.","averageGradient":"45","maxGradient":"105","length":"7.3","correlations":[{"reachID":"1583","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRang